In this conversation, James sought assistance in combining various datasets related to streamflow and meteorological data, including metadata from `grdd-meta.csv`, discharge data from `grdd-data.csv`, and several NetCDF files for temperature and precipitation. I provided a Python-based workflow utilizing `pandas`, `xarray`, and `dask` to consolidate the data into a common dataset organized by station, year, and month. Key steps included loading the datasets, handling time indices correctly, and merging the data while extracting relevant model values. The conversation also addressed creating helper functions to decode NetCDF time attributes and provided detailed coding examples. Ultimately, I ensured the combined dataset included specified columns, suggesting both CSV and Parquet formats for output.
